  - Cost (g4): (260/3600) × 0.798 × 4 = $0.23 ✓
  - Score: 0.23 + (260/7200) × 0.1 = 0.234

SELECTED: 2 × g4 (optimal cost/performance balance)

================================================================================
MOLDABILITY BENEFITS
================================================================================

Static Scheduler:
- Selects (instance_type, num_hosts) once
- Fixed for entire workflow
- Can degrade if resources unavailable
- No adaptation between rounds

Moldable Scheduler:
- Selects (instance_type, num_hosts) initially (same logic)
- Between optimization rounds:
  * Re-runs selectOptimalInstanceType() with updated constraints
  * Can scale UP if more resources available
  * Can scale DOWN if deadline comfortable (save cost)
  * ALL within same instance type (no GPU straggling)
  * Degrades gracefully if optimal not available

Example Moldable Behavior:

Round 1: 8 trials → optimal = 8 × g4
  - Only 4 × g4 available → allocate 4 (degraded)
  - Runtime: 2 batches × 507s = 1014s

Round 2: 4 trials → optimal = 4 × g4
  - All 4 × g4 now available → allocate 4 (fully provisioned)
  - Runtime: 1 batch × 507s = 507s

Round 3: 2 trials → optimal = 2 × g4
  - Scale down: free 2 × g4, keep 2 × g4
  - Runtime: 1 batch × 507s = 507s
  - Cost savings from freed instances!

