================================================================================
LESSONS LEARNED
================================================================================

1. Runtime functions return SINGLE TRIAL time, not total time
   - Must calculate batches when trials > hosts
   - Must account for distributed training when workers > 1

2. Allocation flexibility crucial for moldability
   - Fixed allocations limit scheduler decisions
   - Exploring num_hosts enables cost/performance optimization

3. Resilient allocation better than strict requirements
   - Workflows complete even with degraded resources
   - Better utilization, fewer failures

4. User requirements evolve through discussion
   - Started with simple fix (parallel assumption)
   - Evolved to exploration (Option 4)
   - Refined to resilient + no switching (final)

5. Execution model understanding critical
   - HPO uses Ray Tune with allocate_trials()
   - Different patterns: parallel, sequential, mixed
   - Must account for all cases in runtime calculation

